a":"oṉṟu","gloss":"one"}],"gloss":"any other thing"},{"surface":"இல்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"is not"}],"gloss":"there is not"},{"surface":"எனப்","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"saying"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"sandhi consonant"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பண்","parts":[{"text":"பண்","lemma":"paṇ","gloss":"order/subjection"}],"gloss":"to subjection"},{"surface":"கொளற்கு","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"koḷ","gloss":"take"},{"text":"அற்கு","lemma":"aṟku","gloss":"dative suffix"}],"gloss":"to bring"},{"surface":"அருமை","parts":[{"text":"அருமை","lemma":"arumai","gloss":"difficulty"}],"gloss":"difficulty"},{"surface":"நோக்கி","parts":[{"text":"நோக்கு","lemma":"nōkku","gloss":"look/see"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"seeing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெஞ்சற","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சு","lemma":"neñcu","gloss":"heart"},{"text":"அற","lemma":"aṟa","gloss":"to break/sever"}],"gloss":"with a broken heart"},{"surface":"வீழ்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"வீழ்ந்த","lemma":"வீழ்ந்த","gloss":"who fell"}],"gloss":"who fell","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புரைமை","parts":[{"text":"புரைமை","lemma":"puraimai","gloss":"nobility"}],"gloss":"nobility"},{"surface":"யோனே","parts":[{"text":"யோனே","lemma":"யோனே","gloss":"the noble one indeed"}],"gloss":"the noble one indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"My father who is the support, where is he? / He who fell with the elephant that is like a hill / He appears like a stranger, look there! / Like the tail of a striped squirrel in summer / the old flowers of the forest ūkam shrub that slip and fall / staying in the curled white tubes of the filtered liquor / without giving water and grass, the salt merchants / abandoned in a lonely place with a broken leg / like a great bull that cannot live, the enemies' / great life he takes, and seeing that / the king of the fierce-tempered elephant, in this battlefield / saying 'there is nothing better than dying in battle' / seeing the difficulty of bringing him to order / he who fell with a broken heart, the noble one!","translation":"Where is my father, my support? He who fell alongside the elephant that resembles a hill. Look there, he appears like a stranger! Like the striped tail of a summer squirrel, the old flowers of the forest ūkam shrub slip and fall, staying in the curled white tubes of filtered liquor. Like a great bull abandoned by salt merchants in a lonely place with a broken leg, without water or grass, left to die, he takes the great lives of his enemies. Seeing this, even the king with the fierce-tempered elephant declared, 'There is nothing more glorious than dying in this battlefield,' and seeing how difficult it was to subdue him, the noble warrior fell with a broken heart.","modern":"எனக்கு ஆதாரமாக விளங்கிய என் தந்தை எங்கே இருக்கிறானோ? குன்றைப் போன்ற யானையோடு வீழ்ந்தவன் அவன். இதோ பார், அவன் ஒரு புதியவனைப் போலத் தோன்றுகிறான்! கோடைகாலத்து வரி அணிலின் வால் போன்ற, காட்டில் உள்ள ஊகம் புல்லின் உதிர்ந்து விழும் பழைய பூக்கள், வடித்த கள்ளின் சுருண்ட வெண்மையான குழலில் தங்குவது போல, நீரும் புல்லும் தராமல் உப்பு வணிகர்கள் யாரும் இல்லாத ஒரு பக்கத்தில் முடமான காலுடன் கைவிட்டுச் சென்ற, பிழைக்க முடியாத பெரிய எருதைப் போல, பகைவர்களின் பெரிய உயிரைக் குடிக்கும் அவனைக் கண்டு, கொடிய சினத்தைக் கொண்ட யானையையுடைய வேந்தனும், 'இப்போர்க்களத்தில் இறந்துபடுவதை விடச் சிறந்தது வேறு ஒன்றும் இல்லை' என்று கூறி, அவனை அடக்குவதற்குக் கடினம் என்பதை உணர்ந்து, நெஞ்சு சோர்ந்து வீழ்ந்த பெருமைக்குரியவன் அவன்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Tumpai (battle) landscape, specifically the theme of 'falling alongside the elephant' (kaḷiṟṟuṭaṉilai). The speaker, likely a bard or a close companion, laments the loss of their leader ('my father' or patron) who fought valiantly and died on the battlefield. The poem compares the warrior's relentless assault on his enemies to a dying, abandoned bull that still fights fiercely in its final moments. The imagery of the ūkam flowers falling into the liquor tubes evokes the chaotic and desolate atmosphere of the battlefield. Even the enemy king, witnessing the warrior's indomitable spirit and the impossibility of subduing him, acknowledges his supreme valor before the warrior finally succumbs. Key words include 'ஆசாகு எந்தை' (my father, my support) and 'புரைமையோனே' (the noble one).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.2],[1.2,2.0],[2.0,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,3.8],[3.8,4.4],[4.4,5.34],[5.34,5.9],[5.9,6.3],[6.3,6.5],[6.5,7.28],[7.28,7.8],[7.8,8.2],[8.2,8.94],[8.94,9.5],[9.5,9.87],[9.87,10.43],[10.43,10.57],[10.57,10.8],[10.8,11.4],[11.76,12.0],[12.0,12.4],[12.4,13.0],[13.0,13.6],[13.6,13.9],[13.9,14.1],[14.1,14.5],[14.5,15.7],[15.7,16.0],[16.0,16.58],[16.67,17.0],[17.72,18.32],[18.32,18.77],[18.89,19.22],[19.32,19.62],[19.62,20.22],[20.22,20.42],[20.42,20.72],[20.72,21.02],[21.02,22.09],[22.09,22.62],[22.62,22.92],[22.92,23.82],[23.96,24.92],[24.92,25.42],[25.42,25.72],[25.72,26.02],[26.02,26.47],[26.47,26.84],[26.84,27.22],[27.22,27.52],[27.52,27.88],[27.88,28.37],[28.82,29.22],[29.22,29.48],[29.57,29.92]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.1],[1.1,1.9],[1.9,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,3.5],[3.5,4.1],[4.1,5.4],[5.4,5.85],[5.85,6.2],[6.33,6.73],[6.73,7.21],[7.21,7.7],[7.7,8.1],[8.37,8.5],[8.63,8.9],[8.9,9.47],[9.47,9.66],[9.66,11.0],[11.07,11.23],[11.3,12.2],[12.2,12.8],[12.8,13.3],[13.3,14.0],[14.0,14.7],[14.7,14.9],[14.9,15.1],[15.1,15.6],[15.6,17.0],[17.0,17.3],[17.3,18.1],[18.1,18.5],[19.28,19.88],[19.88,20.45],[20.62,20.98],[21.08,21.38],[21.38,21.82],[21.82,22.26],[22.26,22.48],[22.48,22.88],[22.88,24.01],[24.01,24.58],[24.58,24.98],[24.98,26.18],[26.18,27.38],[27.38,28.08],[28.08,28.48],[28.48,28.84],[28.84,29.22],[29.22,29.48],[29.68,30.08],[30.08,30.58],[30.58,31.02],[31.02,31.61],[31.98,32.48],[32.48,32.68],[32.68,32.98]]},"sync":[[["ஆசாகு","becoming a support"]],[["எந்தை","my father"]],[["யாண்டுளன்","where is he"]],[["கொல்லோ","indeed"]],[["குன்றத்து","of the hill"]],[["அன்ன","like"]],[